				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Posted: Mon Nov 17, 2003 10:29 pm    Post subject: The return to Rallos Zek    
<br />

<br />
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<br />
 
<br />
Vilamil arrived at the druid ring shortly after Kaldarye. In one hand he held a whip and in the other he held tightly onto Keeah's arm. Kaldarye gasped, she hadn't expected him to bring her daughter to the druid portal with him. 
<br />

<br />
Her daughter's face looked puffy as if she'd been crying, her robes were dirty and there was a sheepish look in her eyes. Vilamil thrust Keaah at her and said, “Gate her back to Neriak and put her to bed. She's already been punished. I'll meet you there later tonight and explain where I found her.” 
<br />

<br />
Taking Keeah's hand, Kaldarye gated back to their home. She gave her daughter another long look and resisted the urge to strike her. Kaldarye had never struck her daughter even though it was completely opposite to every single dicate of Tier'dal parentage. She didnt want her daughter to be raised in hate. She had other plans. And now so close to her vengeance goal she wasn't going to give in to her baser tendencies. 
<br />

<br />
“You're going to bed.” Kaldarye said as she helped her daughter out of the robe. Curiously she looked at it as she set it aside, the material was fine, like that of a caster and she made a mental note to ask her daughter where it came from later. 
<br />

<br />
Keeah nodded, gave Kaldarye a tight hug, and went to bed without argument. She looked misrable and was in desperate need of a bath but Kaldarye didn't want her awake when Vil was there. 
<br />

<br />
Once the child was in bed, Kaldarye waited, knowing it wouldn't take long for the rogue to arrive. She heated up some wine and added a little nutmeg and brandy the way he liked it. She hoped a little wine in his blood would dull out his fury.
<br />
