				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Posted: Mon Nov 17, 2003 11:45 pm    Post subject: The return to Rallos Zek    
<br />

<br />
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<br />
 
<br />
Keeah stayed in bed so long the next morning that Kaldarye had to go to her room and look for her. She found her daughter standing next to the window looking outside. 
<br />

<br />
“What are you doing child?” Kaldarye asked. 
<br />

<br />
Keeah jumped and turned around looking guilty. “I was waiting for Uncle Vil to leave.” 
<br />

<br />
“He's not leaving, he's staying here for 2 more days then we're all leaving Legends.” 
<br />

<br />
Keeah looked uneasy. “Where are we going?” 
<br />

<br />
“Home. To Rallos Zek. It's time for you to meet your father. Now get dressed and come to the kitchen.” 
<br />

<br />
“Is Uncle Vil in the kitchen?” her voice was filled with uncharacteristic dread. 
<br />

<br />
“Yes and he's waiting to talk to you.” 
<br />

<br />
Keeah looked nervous. She got dressed so slowly that Kaldarye got impatient and started helping her. Then she grabbed her daughters arm and pulled her to the kitchen. Keeah lagged behind to the point of being a nuisance. Kaldarye jerked her into the room. 
<br />

<br />
Vilamil was sitting at the table waiting like a fat spider in the center of it's web. His face held a strange sardonic grin. And he put a small bag on the table and started dumping its contents out. “Well little one, why don't we start by telling your mother about the items you've been carrying around in this bag.”
<br />
