<br />

<br />
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<br />
 
<br />
It was the night before they were leaving Legends. Kaldarye checked to make sure all her adventuring gear was secure. It had been so long since she'd worn any armor that the steel plate felt stiff and awkward. Her epic seemed unwieldy and a full set of spells felt strange in her head.   Going back to a life of adventuring was a welcome change.  She'd kept a low profile here on legends, with her face being destroyed and her fingers stubbled down from the acid. On Legends appearance meant everything including reputation which is what got you ahead in this dimension of Neriak. Politics were played by the rich pretty people, not by the most spell powerful. Any repairs to her face that the clerics on Legends tried, had failed and she and Vil figured that there wouldn't see permanent improvement til they returned to Rallos. 
<br />

<br />
The idea of returning to Rallos was exciting. Kaldarye had been bored on Legends. Other than the subsequent quickening and birth of her daughter, life had been one long boring day after the next. When Kaldarye first realized she carried another child she had tried to be rid of it. But killing things on Legends was next to impossible and so it had grown inside her. Keeah entered the world on one of the few days the sun broke through the canopy of Nektulos forest. She was born plump, healthy and screaming. Vilamil had taken the babe from the midwife, examined it closely before handing her over to Kaldarye. 
<br />

<br />
“Congrats priestess, she looks like you did when you were a babe.” 
<br />

<br />
“How would you know what I looked like when I was a babe.” Kaldarye had snapped as she took the child. 
<br />

<br />
Vilamil hadn't answered but he gently stroked Keeah's wispy hair and said, “She reminds me of you.” 
<br />

<br />
“I look hideous. My face was destroyed by the acid.” 
<br />

<br />
“That will be remedied when we return. What are you going to call her?” 
<br />

<br />
“Keeah.” 
<br />

<br />
“Why?” 
<br />

<br />
“It was the name of Greon's sister.” 
<br />

<br />
He was curious. “You hold Greon's sister in regard?” 
<br />

<br />
“No. But she was someone who is more hideous looking than me.” 
<br />

<br />
Vilamil harrumphed. “Priestess you are evil.” 
<br />

<br />
“You said the child looked like me. Now she has a name to match.” 
<br />

<br />
Vil took the child out of Kaldarye's arms are held it up. “Her eyes are the crystalline blue of your clan ancestors. It is a good omen. She will be a credit to your name.” 
<br />

<br />
“If I keep her.” Kaldarye had muttered under her breath. 
<br />

<br />
Keeah's birth had been years ago. Funny Kaldarye hadn't thought of it til now as she tramped in the streets towards the home of Malsqueek the Enchanter. The enchanter had dared think he could interfere in her plans for her daughter. Now he would pay. 
<br />

<br />

<br />
Malsqueek's house was a large stone structure with sloped curving roofs, a dozen pipe chimneys, small dark-glazed windows and a single entry into the front door. Never one for subtlety Kaldarye walked up to the door intending to stun and smite whoever opened it, completely forgetting she wasnt' on Rallos Zek and unable to slay them.
<br />
