				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Posted: Sat Nov 22, 2003 3:37 pm    Post subject: The Return to Rallos Zek    
<br />

<br />
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<br />
 
<br />
Vilamil had one last thing to do before he left legends. He was going to open a cross channel to Rallos. He leaned back and closed his eyes. Talking to another realm was mentally draining and he wanted this conversation to go as quickly as possible so he could conserve energy. He'd never actually spoken to the recipient of his message before and he hoped his channel was well received. If it wasn't received, then their exit from Legends would be delayed a few days while he made other plans. 
<br />

<br />
Whatever happened he couldn't let Kaldarye take control of the child once they returned. The last thing he wanted was for Kald to march Keeah straight away to Tramplebrey and the blood temple. Kaldarye had been acting irrational as of late, the same way she had behaved when they'd first arrived on Legends and Vilamil was sure it was due to her being pregnant again. There was something about a tier'dal female that made them think they were invincible when their hormones were raging. Vilamil had seen the same thing in Kaldarye's mother long long ago. 
<br />

<br />
He sighed. If his fate and Kaldarye's weren't so irrevocably intertwined he'd be tempted to leave her behind. It would be much easier to leave her on Legends than to take her back. 
<br />

<br />
Breaking a channel to Rallos Zek was difficult and for almost half an hour Vilamil was concerned that the recipient was asleep. Waking up someone from Legends never had good results and Vilamil was reluctant to do so. Breaking off the attempt he decided to check up on his charges before trying again. 
<br />

<br />
Keeah, the little one, had finially gotten over her fear of him since he'd whipped her in Plane of Knowledge and was back to her happy buoyant self. She was even playing with that silly doll she carried around with her. Vil knew he'd have to reinstill that fear of him when they returned to Rallos but until they made the crossing that could wait. 
<br />

<br />
Peering into her room he was surprised to see she wasn't in bed. Probably she was pestering Kaldarye again about going to visit her “enslaved friends” one last time before they left. She'd been bothering Kaldarye about it all evening to the point that it was even getting on his nerves. He'd had to leave the cottage in order to avoid smacking the child into silence. 
<br />

<br />
When he looked into Kaldarye's room he knew something was wrong. Neither Kaldarye or her daughter were there. Worse Kaldarye's trunk of armor had been emptied. 
<br />

<br />
Swearing an oath to Innoruuk, Vilamil opened a channed to Rallos to the first tier'dal member of No Tears he could find. “Anuxiree, tell Greon to be available to take a channel from Legends. I have important information about his wife.” 
<br />

