<br />
 
<br />
Ten months! It had been almost a year and Greon had almost given up hope of hearing of anything about his wife. 
<br />

<br />
He had sent Longinius, his guild mate and House Captain of the guards, off to every city that he could walk unmolested, to gain the confidence of guards and glean any gossip that he could. 
<br />

<br />
Likewise, Qrom, dwarven miner and finder of things lost and not yet lost, took himself off to mine information of the lost woman and child through his contacts with the thieves Guild of various and sundry citys. 
<br />

<br />
No one had found any information, no one had heard any whisper or boast of the coup. 
<br />

<br />
It had seemed that Kaldarye had dropped off the face of the world and their child, stolen by the Hand, had also. 
<br />

<br />
Greon seriously doubted that the two were once more united. 
<br />
The Hand had no use for Kaldarye, and she no use or interest in the child. 
<br />

<br />
Other then systematically hunting down and killing every member of the Hand's people, Greon was at a loss for justice. 
<br />

<br />
And now this. Who was this Vilamil... oh. Him. 
<br />

<br />
Greon winced in remembrance. Vilamil was Kaldarye's minion who was in on the humiliating "wedding" he was forced into. In fact, it was that rogue who had darted him with the poison that had paralyzed him for several days. 
<br />

<br />
And now he was wanting to talk. Well, this should be interesting. 
<br />

<br />
Greon held in check the flare of hope.
<br />
