				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Posted: Wed Dec 10, 2003 7:02 pm    Post subject: The return to Rallos Zek    
<br />

<br />
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<br />
 
<br />
Vilamil glanced at the recently set-off trap on the front door one last time before he crept around the side of the house towards the back. The guards were still pacing and bored, completely oblivious that a rogue was in their midst. Vilamil gave the brush a thorough look to make sure someone else wasn't watching him before he settled himself into the small cubby he'd previously dug out near the phosflurescent lichen bush to receive the tell. 
<br />

<br />
"Greetings. You have information regarding my wife?" Greon's voice filling his mind had a guarded hopefulness. 
<br />

<br />
"You wife is on Legends." 
<br />

<br />
"Ka'Seth" Greon replied in an ancient curse. "No wonder I couldn't find her. And our child? Was it also removed to that realm?" 
<br />

<br />
Vilamil knew Greon was referring to the male child the Hated Ones had stolen - who was also here on Legends but neither Greon nor Kaldarye needed to know that information. Not after the moral undisciplined way Vilamil had watched Kaldarye raise her daughter. Headstrong, innocent, smiling unabused little Keaah was not the child Greon was expecting at all. "Her little one is here with her." he replied vaguely. 
<br />

<br />
An audible sigh of relief filled his head. "They are both well then?" 
<br />

<br />
Vilamil hesitated in his reply. He wouldn't call Kaldarye well. She was ghastly ugly. The female trolls in his guild were more pleasing to the eye. They'd been on legends for years now and even after all this time he still hadn't gotten used to looking at her. The acid Tramplebrey had used on her face had done it's job well. More often than naught he found himself looking away or over her shoulder to avoid meeting her eyes. It sickened him what Tramplebrey had done. The prelate would have been a long dead elf if it hadn't been for Vilamil's carefully laid other plans. He curled his fingers around his dagger. He could have bought 2 bard speed horses with the money he'd spent on legends paying out clerics trying to get Kaldarye's face restored, not to mention the time he'd spent searching down items to improve her charisma, even trading items to gnome tinkers for help. All for naught. "Your wife and her child will both be unrecognizable to you. I'll let you be the judge on her well-being when I return." 
<br />

<br />
“You are returning to Rallos Zek?” Greon's voice was cautious, slightly hopeful. 
<br />

<br />
“I'll leave her in your care tomorrow night.” 
<br />

<br />
"Why are you doing this? I know you are in her employ, I remember you from the wedding," his voice was full of suspicion and hostility. 
<br />

<br />
"Because your house is the last place her enemies will look.” 
<br />

<br />
“You mean the Temple of Blood and her family, House N'Bane.” the hatred in Greon's voice was almost audible. 
<br />

<br />
“Yes. I 've had people watching them and you in the months we've been gone. The powers of Neriak consider your house a non-entity. In their eyes the loss of your wife has destroyed your importance in Innoruuk's game.” 
<br />

<br />
“The power of Neriak will never totally disregard me. Innoruuk will not allow it.” Greon replied angrily. 
<br />

<br />
“In time you will once again their notice. But for now you will be left alone as long as Kaldarye is believed to be missing/dead. I trust you have the means to keep her and her child there out of reach of the blood temple?" 
<br />

<br />
"Yes, I think so." 
<br />

<br />
"No one must know she's returned. The fingers and eyes of the blood temple are everywhere, including your own temple. Take care whom you trust." 
<br />

<br />
Greon sounded flustered. "Who are you? What do you expect to get? what is your price?” 
<br />

<br />
Ignoring the question, Vilamil's attention focused on the back of the house where the guards were dragging an unconscious individual outside. He moved fowards towards the iron gate and watched as they hoisted the limp battered body up over the back of the air elemental. The body groaned and rolled slightly giving him full view of it's horridly mutilated face. 
<br />

<br />
"Stupid pregnant Kaldarye." Vilamil accidently sent in tell to Greon as he recognized the unconscious distorted face of Kaldarye. 
<br />

<br />
"I beg your pardon." Greon replied sounding confused. 
<br />

<br />
"Just Be ready for her tomorrow night." Vilamil snarled as he ended the tell. 
<br />

<br />

