<br />

<br />
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<br />
 
<br />
The morning sun peaked over the Surefall horizon, the jagged line of peaks and pine trees that define the Glade. In the cabin by Surefall Pond Micheall was finishing the morning dishes. The near mindless tasks assigned by Hagar done once more, poachers killed and heads spiked, beating back the Griffawns in Nedaria's Landing, helping the Wayfarer's Brotherhood accomplish their tasks by supplying them with the meat of turtles and panthers. 
<br />

<br />
Since he had left the company of his guild, he had served the Brotherhood of Rangers at Surefall, teaching fletching to the younger rangers, being a glorified game warden, occasional simple smithing tasks. His diligence at his tasks assured him a place in the Glade, even as his brothers and masters encouraged him to return to the world, adventure and grow in his skills. Someday perhaps. He had been mourning his family for three years now, the cousin kidnapped and corrupted from her faith in Karana, forced to marry the hated dark elf. Then killed when he grew bored with her. Her parents, his aunt and uncle who had all but raised him when his own parents were killed by gnolls, who both died of grief within months of their only daughter. Her two younger brothers had been killed in an ill advised storming of the gates of Neriak, along with several young Knights of Marr and Thunder recruited by a madman set on adventure. 
<br />

<br />
He knows it is time to reenter the world, but still he hesitates, waiting for a sign, wanting to return to the life of adventure he once knew but not knowing if he still had the heart for it. 
<br />

<br />
The door to the cabin opens, an adventurer walks in, wearing the trappings of a wealthy enchantress. She spots Micheall and walks over to him. As always, obedient to the dictates of his oaths, he asks what he can do to help her. 
<br />

<br />
She takes his hand, brings it to his face, and says "You do not remember me Micheall? The evening we spent in The Lion's Mane so long ago?" 
<br />

<br />
Startled, drawn back, he stutters "Lady Merksa, what are you doing here, you can't stay, they will kill you without hesitation if they discover who you are." 
<br />

<br />
Smiling softly, she looks into his eyes. "Don't worry Micheall, they have all been calmed, none of them think I am anything but the human lady I appear to be. But if it would comfort you, go to Qeynos for the afternoon, I am still welcome there. Meet me at the Lion's Mane, for old times sake." With that, she faded away, a soft pop heard as the space she once occupied filled with air. 
<br />

<br />
After making sure his plans to be absent for the rest of the day were known to Hagar, he began the short run to Qeynos, well short because of the Spirit of the Wolf. He passed by the lake in the Qeynos Hills and saw Axe, Rephas and Hadden making one of his brief appearances. He stopped by the bank making sure he had enough coin to buy a meal and a few rounds of drinks for the two of them. He knew quite well Merksa never carried any coin and he preferred to pay for things rather than have her try to charm the merchants. Things had changed since the old days, the Order of Three supplied all the merchants with charms to prevent the magics ensorceling them and having them give their stock away for nothing. 
<br />

<br />
He met her once more, now disguised as an Erudite, at the Lion's Mane, they ordered a late lunch and talked about old times. Then, after avoiding the reason for her visit for an hour, she looked at Micheall and asked "Will you return to us Micheall. We have need of you." 
<br />

<br />
"I still mourn my family, I cannot hunt alongside Greon. His actions are unexcusable, unforgivable, even in his madness. I am the last of her family that still remembers Moireen, he has killed not only her, but all her family. The joy-filled Micheall you knew is long dead." 
<br />

<br />
"No Micheall, you still live, your soul still thrives in the woodlands, you still craft remarkable things. Your grief has crippled you for so long, you forget who you were, who you are. You inspired so many of our people to achieve greatness in the crafts. You have always underestimated your effect on people, being the hermit of a ranger you are. Please come back to us." 
<br />

<br />
"What would you have me do Merksa, you are all skilled in so many areas. Earenhylle is feared throughout Norrath. Elaynia has become the bane of the psychopathic wanderers that plague the world. Greon has achieved fame throughout the lands, and is among the most skilled if least sane healers in Norrath. Chernabog has mastered everything I did and more, you yourself have an unparallelled reputation in making the finest jewelry in the realms. What do I really have to offer the guild at this point." 
<br />

<br />
"If you rejoin us we will make sure you gain experience quickly, that your skills and equipment grow quickly to match the rest of us. You have the talents, the mind to do it. Of all the fighters I have known, your mind was the brightest, the warmest of them all. You will once more be able to pursue your dream of crafting the finest treasures in the world. You are wasted here in Qeynos, at the Glade. Come live the way of No Tears again, and pursue the adventure you always loved." 
<br />

<br />
"And Greon, what of him. I have never known a cleric so eager to watch a comrade die just so he could practice resurrecting them. I will not fight alongside him." 
<br />

<br />
"Greon has changed, in some ways for the better. He has vowed he will not attack you first. However he is one of the reasons I am here." 
<br />

<br />
"Does he need me to recover his body from a place he shouldn't have gone again? How could I go anyplace you couldn't? He always claimed I gave bad directions when he couldn't tell his left from his right. Do you know that one time I marked his gloves left and right so that he could tell which way to turn. He took them off because he was warm, and immediately got lost again." 
<br />

<br />
"No, but for now I need you to keep something for awhile. It concerns Greon, and his family. No one knows I have it, and I have to be able to say I do not have it and have no idea where it is, truthfully." She passed a small but substantial pouch under the table, a move Micheall remembered well. She leaned up to him, kissed his cheek and said "It is sealed with the ancient Tier'Dal blood runes, they will kill anyone who tries to open the bag without the proper spells." She then pressed her hand into his and left a smaller pouch in his hand when she withgdrew hers. "Take those and sell them, you will need some new gear, and your weapons are sturdy but old, see if you can find something more suitable for my ranger to wield." 
<br />

<br />
"I will consider your offer Merksa, and I will safeguard your items. None will know I have them or where they are." 
<br />

<br />
As she faded away once more, Micheall wondered how much of what she said was real, and how much was merely illusion. He took the sealed pouch she had given him and hid it in his cloak. Time to visit Gash and Garin, and perhaps say a few prayers at the Temple of Thunder before heading home to the Glade. He looked in the smaller pouch, saw several sapphires sparkling brightly. 
<br />

<br />
Later on he wondered, was it even Merksa, it sounded like her and she knew things only Merksa would know, but he hadn't seen her in her born form, only illusions. Before she reclaimed the pouch, she would have to show him the scars he knew she had, in the places no one would see them.
<br />
_________________
