<br />
It took Vilamil almost 20 minutes to take down all the traps and bypass the guards and slip inside the house of Malsqueek the enchanter. The first sound he heard when he entered was Keeah screaming. It sounded as if she was being tortured. Putting aside caution, Vilamil moved towards the sound of her voice. He found her on the third floor in a small denlike room cowering as a male and female tier'dal beat her. It was the kind of beating that would leave marks unless a cleric healed it. Forcing himself to stop at the entrance of the room, Vilamil watched and listened. 
<br />

<br />
And was horrified to learn that Keeah had been tricked into willingly putting on a collar of submission binding her to the enchanter forever. Swearing an oath to Innoruuk, Vilamil backed out of the room and weighed his options. Perhaps Keeah deserved what had happened to her but Kaldarye would never return to Rallos Zek without the child. And as long as Malsqueek was alive and determined to keep the child, Keeah could never return. He was not going back to Rallos Zek without Kaldarye. His own plans would be ruined should she not return. And the time for both of them to return was running out. He had to try and get this resolved quickly. 
<br />

<br />
As much as he hated the idea, there was really only once choice in getting the child her freedom. He'd have to duel the enchanter.
